  "body": "## What changed\n\nThrough holes ran a hidden, fixed 1.0 mm past the part bottom (`THROUGH_CLEAR`; one pitch on a thread), not a parameter and not checked against what is under the part. Now:\n\n- **A stated parameter.** Drill, Bore and Thread carry `break_through: Option<f64>` (mm). `None` is the kind's old figure - 1.0 mm for Drill and Bore, one pitch for an internal Thread - so every existing op generates and posts byte-identical and keeps its digest (written only when stated). It is a **Break-through** row (Default / a length in the document unit) in the hole kinds' Heights > Levels group, `break_through` in the project file and in the MCP params JSON (`add_operation` / `edit_operation` read the same DTO).\n- **Kernels:** `drilling::CycleParams::through_clear`, `machining2d::ThreadParams::through_run`; the Bore already took `through_allowance`, now the op's value (and Detect holes' borability reads it too).\n- **Said:** every op with a through hole notes `through holes run 1.000 mm past the part bottom (Break-through), the deepest to Z...` in the document unit.\n- **Checked against what lies below:** with workholding or a table modelled in the setup, the fixture laws judge the tip - a break-through into modelled steel is a `FixtureHit` on the flute and holds the post (pinned with a spoil board modelled under the stock); air between modelled parallels stays legal. With nothing modelled, a tip under the stock bottom is **named, not refused**: `Break-through below stock: the through hole at (x, y) runs to Z.., .. under the stock bottom Z.. - whatever the stock sits on is cut there; model the parallels, spoil board or fixture under it ..., or lower the Break-through`. Refusing there would stop every through hole in a plate sawn to size, a program that posts today; the reasoning is in `docs/decisions/1557-through-break-through.md`.\n- Negative / non-finite values are refused at creation (`sane`) and by the kernels; a stated value on a lathe's axial or cross Drill is refused by name.\n- **Project file v63** (`PROJECT_VERSION` 62 -> 63): an old reader must refuse a file rather than drop a stated break-through. If another open PR also takes v63, whichever merges second takes the next number.\n\n## How tested\n\n- New `crates/app/tests/break_through.rs`: `the_default_is_today_s_millimetre_and_is_said` (Drill and Bore: deepest Z -1.000, note, below-stock note), `a_stated_break_through_moves_the_deepest_feed` (0.3 mm and 0 for Drill, 0.3 for Bore), `a_negative_break_through_is_refused_at_creation`, `a_break_through_into_modelled_steel_under_the_stock_is_refused` (flute hit, post refused; 0 posts), `the_parameter_round_trips_the_file_and_the_mcp_params`.\n- `operation::break_through` unit tests (deepest tip, below-stock note with and without steel, inch document).\n- `machining2d::thread_tests::a_through_hole_runs_one_pitch_unless_the_break_through_is_stated`.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green (motion 455 s, app 1145 s, ui 65 s); `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- The user's end-cap project (a copy, `camcraft-cli process ... -o`): 8 ops ok, gate ok, the posted program is **byte-identical** to the v0.21.0 program (its four holes are `through: false` with a typed floor, so no break-through applies).\n\n## UI evidence\n\nThe shipping shell renders the Drill, Bore and Thread Heights pages below. Before captures omit the new Break-through row (the pre-change page). After captures show the default and an explicit length. PNGs live only on the fork's images-only `pr-screenshots` branch.\n\n| Page | Before | After, default | After, stated mm |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Drill | [Before](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/ae6183eb/2126/drill-before.png) | [After](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/ae6183eb/2126/drill-after.png) | [Stated](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/ae6183eb/2126/drill-stated-mm.png) |\n| Bore | [Before](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/ae6183eb/2126/bore-before.png) | [After](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/ae6183eb/2126/bore-after.png) | [Stated](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/ae6183eb/2126/bore-stated-mm.png) |\n| Thread | [Before](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/ae6183eb/2126/thread-before.png) | [After](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/ae6183eb/2126/thread-after.png) | [Stated](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/ae6183eb/2126/thread-stated-mm.png) |\n\nStructural pins: `hole_break_through_default_controls_and_document_units` checks the Default checkbox, default text, explicit numeric field and mm/in unit lens for all three kinds, restores Default, and checks Heights-only placement. `external_thread_has_no_hole_break_through_control` checks external threads. Removing the row calls makes the first pin RED; restoring them makes both GREEN.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A tool-relative default (drill point length): not added, see the decision file.\n- Lathe axial and cross holes keep `THROUGH_CLEAR` (a stated value is refused there).\n\nChangelog: Drill, Bore and Thread state their through-hole Break-through (default 1.0 mm, one pitch for a thread; unchanged programs post identically); the op notes how far past the part bottom it runs and names a run under an unmodelled stock bottom; project file v63\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1557\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n\n",
